  su name module manuscript segment one retry request role stage ob text "ROLE:\nSegment 1 establishes the system. Define it clearly and explain the basic mechanism.\n\nTARGET_WORDS:\n85-100\n\nGOAL_WORDS:\n90\n\nPOSITIVE_RULES:\nStay mainly with SEED CONCEPT and CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE. Prefer affirmative declarative language that says what the system is and how it works.\n\nOPTIONAL_ADD_ONS:\nYou may include one small example from AFFAIRS OR ACTIVITIES when it helps ground the segment. If you use an example, keep it brief and supportive rather than letting it become the paragraph's main job. Practice language is acceptable when it stays inside a simple illustration of how the teaching works. You may include one small immediate implication when it follows naturally from the definition and mechanism.\n\nNEGATIVE_RULES:\nAvoid negation-led or contrast-led phrasing like not, rather than, instead of, unlike, or however. If the source carries a contrast, translate it into a positive sentence about what the thing is or does. Keep scarcity, domination, blockage, counterfeit, or misunderstanding language out of the paragraph's main establish move when the source offers a cleaner affirmative lane. Prefer the fallible-service and raw-material/perfect-possibility frame before channel, transparent-vessel, or flow language. Do not introduce hidden contradictions, jump to large consequences, or turn the segment into a correction of misunderstanding.\n\nFEEDBACK:\nGenerate a fresh Segment 1 from the source and verifier feedback, not from the failed draft. Write about 90 words, and keep the result between 88 and 94 words. Use complete sentences. Cut before adding. If the section starts getting long, remove extra restatement instead of adding another explanation.\n\nSOURCE_THRUST_FEEDBACK:\n" to name text module manuscript segment one retry request be text do
